imguru v1.0.7 by Roland Rabien (figbug@gmail.com) Nov  2 2026.

usage: imguru [-odpilmbdhvcanwx] [-s max_dimension] source_file ...
Uploads one of more images to imgur.com. Supports all image formats supported by Mac OS X and will resize and convert to JPEG before uploading.

-d  Display direct link to image (default)
-p  Display link to image page
-i  Display HTML image
-l  Display HTML link
-c  Also copy link to clipboard
-m  Display message board image code
-b  Display message board link code
-o  Open uploaded images in browser
-s  Resize image to have maximum dimension of max_dimension
-a  Sign in to an imgur account, uploads then go to it
-n  Upload anonymously even when signed in
-w  Show which account imguru is signed in to
-x  Sign out
-h  Display help
-v  Display version

Accounts:
By default uploads are anonymous, which means they are not tied to any account
and cannot be deleted or listed afterwards.

Run "imguru -a" to sign in. It opens imgur in your browser, you allow access,
and imgur shows you a PIN to paste back into the terminal. After that every
upload goes to your account until you run "imguru -x". Use "imguru -n" for a
one off anonymous upload, and "imguru -w" to see who you are signed in as.

Credentials are stored in ~/.imguru as key=value lines, readable only by you.
The access token is refreshed automatically when it expires.

Signing in needs the api client secret, which is not kept in this repository.
Released builds have it compiled in. If you build from source and want to sign
in, add a line to ~/.imguru:

  client_secret=your_secret_here

or set IMGUR_CLIENT_SECRET in the environment. Without it imguru still works,
it just uploads anonymously. Note that imgur no longer registers new api
clients, so every copy of imguru shares one client id and its rate limits.

Depends on:
imgur.com
tinyxml
curl
NSImage+MGCropExtensions

Download:
https://github.com/FigBug/imguru/releases/download/v1.0.7/imguru.zip
